{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794316137551,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7164a0ffeGzBXMRKesHHNFV","part":{"id":"prt_1c5937409001Wd661ggnzicbJr","messageID":"msg_1c5935f7f0015UbCIeaMdajyUC","sessionID":"ses_e3a7164a0ffeGzBXMRKesHHNFV","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794316137551,"sessionID":"ses_e3a7164a0ffeGzBXMRKesHHNFV","part":{"id":"prt_1c593740e001wDhmzPWUBSTXhv","messageID":"msg_1c5935f7f0015UbCIeaMdajyUC","sessionID":"ses_e3a7164a0ffeGzBXMRKesHHNFV","type":"text","text":"Done. Built the full account service with password reset.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): SQLite storage with `accounts`, `sessions`, `reset_tokens`, and `outbox` tables. PBKDF2 password hashing, opaque bearer tokens (SHA-256 hashed at rest), case-insensitive unique emails, single-use reset tokens with a 1-hour TTL. All required endpoints implemented, plus `GET /api/health` and static frontend serving.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src/`): React + TypeScript with Tailwind v4 and react-router — sign-in/register forms, account page (email edit + change-password), \"Forgot password?\" form, `/reset` token page, and a Mailbox page.\n\nVerified via Flask test client: registration/login/me/patch/password-change, full reset flow (outbox link → confirm → invalidate), case-insensitive email uniqueness, no-email reset no-op, short-password rejection, and 401 handling. `npm run build` passes.\n\nNote: the repo's `requirements.lock` has stale hashes that break `pip install -c`; the Docker build will fail until it's regenerated. Let me know if you'd like me to regenerate it.","time":{"start":1794316137486,"end":1794316137491}}}
